# Design system (DESIGN.md)

Read project-root `DESIGN.md` before generating or editing any visual UI. YAML front matter is normative for tokens; Markdown sections are how to apply them.

## Apply from DESIGN.md

- **Colors** - use only defined tokens/roles (semantic name + hex + usage). Do not invent palette entries.
- **Typography** - follow type roles and pairings; do not default to Inter/system unless the file allows it.
- **Layout / Spacing** - respect the spacing scale and layout model.
- **Shapes / Elevation** - match radius and depth language (rules/tonal layers vs heavy shadow).
- **Components** - implement documented variants and states (`default`, `hover`, `focus`, `disabled`, plus `error` / loading when specified). Missing states → inventing per-file patterns is a defect.
- **Do's and Don'ts** - never violate this section.

Prefer CSS custom properties / existing project styling that map to these tokens. Framework utilities must resolve to the same values.

## Spacecraft authority

- House look SoT: root `DESIGN.md` when present.
- After `/sc-discuss` approval, mission look SoT is `[data-draft-surface]` in the approved draft - **port** structure, tokens, spacing, type, and chrome; do not freestyle a second look.
- House vs proposed style conflict → stop; record exactly one of `DESIGN conflict: mission exception | update house | keep house` in `decisions.md` before drafting/implementing.
- Anti-slop catalog (sc-ux-design) wins over vague aesthetic preference unless an exception is recorded.
- Visual product UI needs draft approval (or a recorded non-visual skip). No mid-build competing design system.

## Missing or ambiguous DESIGN.md

- Missing → produce a candidate via `/sc-discuss` + sc-ux-design design brief; do not silently invent house tokens in product code.
- Ambiguous token → prefer `name (#hex): usage` specificity; tighten `DESIGN.md` rather than guessing.
